{%- liquid
  assign desktop_image = section.settings.image
  assign mobile_image = section.settings.image_mobile | default: desktop_image
  assign use_performance_hero = false
  if desktop_image.src contains 'pexels-taryn-elliott-4112233.jpg' and mobile_image.src contains 'pexels-taryn-elliott-4112236_2.jpg'
    assign use_performance_hero = true
  endif
-%}

<section class="en-hero" dir="rtl" aria-labelledby="en-hero-title-{{ section.id }}">
  <div class="en-hero__media" aria-hidden="true">
    {%- if desktop_image != blank -%}
      <picture>
        {%- if use_performance_hero -%}
          <source media="(max-width: 749px)" srcset="{{ 'elmsnest-hero-mobile-performance.webp' | asset_url }}">
          <img src="{{ 'elmsnest-hero-desktop-performance.webp' | asset_url }}" width="1456" height="768" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" alt="">
        {%- else -%}
          {%- if mobile_image != blank -%}
            <source media="(max-width: 749px)" srcset="{{ mobile_image | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w, {{ mobile_image | image_url: width: 640 }} 640w, {{ mobile_image | image_url: width: 760 }} 760w, {{ mobile_image | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w" sizes="100vw">
          {%- endif -%}
          {{ desktop_image | image_url: width: 1920 | image_tag: loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high', widths: '900,1200,1600,1920', sizes: '100vw', alt: '' }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </picture>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
  <span class="en-hero__shade" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  {%- comment -%}
    Two purely decorative layers that play the moment a solar fixture exists
    for: dusk falls, the cell has charged, the lamps come on. Both are
    aria-hidden and carry no content of their own.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <span class="en-hero__glow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="en-hero__dusk" aria-hidden="true"></span>

  <div class="en-hero__wrap">
    <div class="en-hero__content">

      <h1 id="en-hero-title-{{ section.id }}">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h1>

      {%- comment -%}
        The rating plate. Every value below is transcribed from the product
        specification sections the store already publishes, never inferred.
        Adding a value here without a source in the catalogue breaks the
        brand's own first principle.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <dl class="en-plate" aria-label="נתוני מפרט מתוך עמודי המוצרים בקטלוג">
        <div class="en-plate__cell">
          <dt>עמידות</dt>
          <dd><bdi dir="ltr">IP65</bdi></dd>
        </div>
        <div class="en-plate__cell">
          <dt>גוון אור</dt>
          <dd><bdi dir="ltr">3000K</bdi></dd>
        </div>
        <div class="en-plate__cell">
          <dt>שעות תאורה</dt>
          <dd><bdi dir="ltr">8–10</bdi></dd>
        </div>
        <div class="en-plate__cell">
          <dt>חיווט חשמל</dt>
          <dd><bdi dir="ltr">0</bdi></dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      {%- comment -%}
        Scope line. The plate's four values are each licensed by a published
        product page, but the catalogue also holds 2700K, IP67 and wired
        models — presenting them unscoped claimed a uniformity the catalogue
        contradicts one click later.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="en-plate__scope">נתונים מתוך מפרטי מוצרים בחנות · המפרט המלא של כל דגם — בעמוד המוצר</p>

      {%- if section.settings.text != blank -%}<div class="en-hero__text">{{ section.settings.text }}</div>{%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        The two buttons answer two different states of mind: the visitor who
        knows what they want goes to the catalogue; the visitor who does not
        goes to the choosing guide. The council flagged the previous pair for
        pointing at the same section under two labels.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="en-hero__actions">
        <a class="en-hero__primary" href="#elmsnest-home-products">{{ section.settings.primary_label }}</a>
        <a class="en-hero__secondary" href="{{ section.settings.secondary_url | default: pages['guide-garden-lighting'].url | default: '#elmsnest-home-shop' }}">{{ section.settings.secondary_label }}</a>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Fit-to-place is the buying decision, so the four collections are
        presented as a ruled schedule of places, not as decorative pills.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <nav class="en-hero__places" aria-label="קולקציות תאורת חוץ">
        {%- comment -%}
          Labels come from the collections themselves, never from a hand-written
          string: a hand-written label drifts from the catalogue and starts making
          claims the collection cannot keep. "תאורת קיר סולארית" was one — only one
          of its six products is solar. The index must name what it opens.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign place_handles = 'תאורת-שביל-סולארית,solar-wall-lights,ספוטים-ופרוז-קטורים-סולאריים,גרילנדות-ותאורה-דקורטיבית' | split: ',' -%}
        {%- for place_handle in place_handles -%}
          {%- assign place = collections[place_handle] -%}
          {%- if place != blank and place.products_count > 0 -%}
            <a href="{{ place.url }}"><span>{{ place.title }}</span></a>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </nav>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
.en-hero,.en-hero *{box-sizing:border-box}
/* Kalles sets the root font size to 10px, so every rem here resolved at 62.5%
   of what it was written for: `44rem` was meant to be 704px and rendered 440.
   The column was half the width intended, which is what pushed the headline to
   three lines and squeezed the schedule cells to 110px. Lengths on this section
   are px from here on — a rem in this theme does not mean what it reads. */
.en-hero{
  --plate-rule:rgb(var(--en-ink)/.30);
  position:relative;display:flex;min-height:min(88vh,760px);
  direction:rtl;background:rgb(var(--en-night));color:rgb(var(--en-ink));
  overflow:hidden;isolation:isolate
}
.en-hero__media{position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:-4}
/* Two art-directed assets share this element: a 1456x768 landscape (desktop,
   native resolution — the 960px pathway source could only ever deliver a third
   of the pixels a full-bleed 1440 band needs) and a 560x1046 portrait band of
   the pathway shot (mobile). Both are graded down so the lamps stay the
   brightest thing on screen; mobile gets a lighter grade below because the
   full-coverage content plus this grade read as a black rectangle in testing.
   object-position keeps each subject lamp in frame when cover crops the sides
   (>1440 desktop, 640-749 phablet): the lamp heads sit in the upper third. */
.en-hero__media img{
  width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:50% 30%;display:block;
  filter:brightness(.66) contrast(1.08) saturate(.88)
}
@media(max-width:749px){
  .en-hero__media img{filter:brightness(.8) contrast(1.08) saturate(.88)}
}

/* Darkest on the reading side. `to left` is physical and the section is RTL,
   so the first stop lands on the right, under the content. The council found
   the previous build mixing a logical margin with a physical gradient, which
   put the text over the brightest part of the photograph. */
.en-hero__shade{
  position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:-3;
  background:
    linear-gradient(to left,rgb(var(--en-night)/.94) 0%,rgb(var(--en-night)/.82) 40%,rgb(var(--en-night)/.52) 76%,rgb(var(--en-night)/.40) 100%),
    linear-gradient(to top,rgb(var(--en-night)/.82) 0%,rgb(var(--en-night)/.18) 52%,transparent 100%)
}

/* The section sits under a transparent header (Kalles pulls it up by
   --header-height), so the first line has to clear the nav on its own. */
/* The section must not fill the viewport exactly. Half of visitors never
   scroll at all, and a first screen that looks finished is read as finished —
   so the terms strip below has to show its top edge unprompted. The rhythm
   here is tuned to leave that edge visible at 1440x900 and 390x844; if content
   is added to the hero, re-measure rather than assume it still fits. */
.en-hero__wrap{
  width:min(1200px,100%);margin-inline:auto;
  padding:calc(var(--header-height,0px) + var(--top-bar-height,0px) + clamp(28px,3.4vw,52px)) clamp(18px,4vw,40px) clamp(26px,3.6vw,56px)
}
.en-hero__content{max-width:700px}

.en-hero h1{
  margin:0;color:rgb(var(--en-ink));
  /* No negative tracking on Hebrew display text. Tightening is a Latin habit —
     it buys density there because Latin has open counters and a long x-height
     run. Hebrew letters hang from the top line with tight counters already, and
     W3C hlreq names letter-spacing as Hebrew's EXPANSION tool for emphasis, the
     substitute for a case distinction the script does not have. Compressing it
     spends that tool in the wrong direction. */
  font-size:clamp(34px,5.4vw,64px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:normal;font-weight:700;
  text-wrap:balance
}

/* The rating plate: a ruled instrument panel, not a stat row. Amber is spent
   on measured values only — never on a control, a rule, or a hover state — so
   that seeing it anywhere on the page means "this number was measured". */
/* Near-solid ground: at .86 the bright lantern pixels behind the plate bled
   through and worst-pixel contrast under the labels dropped to 1.4-2.5:1
   (detector finding, 2026-08-14). The plate is an instrument face, not a
   glass card — it may sit ON the photo, never let the photo through it. */
.en-plate{
  display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));
  margin:clamp(16px,2.2vw,24px) 0 0;padding:0;
  border:1px solid var(--plate-rule);
  background:rgb(var(--en-night)/.97)
}
.en-plate__cell{padding:14px 16px;border-inline-start:1px solid var(--plate-rule)}
.en-plate__cell:first-child{border-inline-start:0}
.en-plate dt{
  margin:0 0 7px;color:rgb(var(--en-ink)/.92);
  /* The eyebrow role. In Latin this line would be uppercase; on Hebrew that
     declaration measures 0.00px, so the whole distinction has to be carried by
     weight and tracking instead. This is the sanctioned direction. */
  font-size:12px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:.04em
}
.en-plate dd{
  margin:0;color:rgb(var(--en-amber));
  font-size:clamp(22px,2.6vw,30px);font-weight:700;line-height:1;
  font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;letter-spacing:-.02em
}
.en-plate__scope{margin:8px 0 0;color:rgb(var(--en-ink)/.60);font-size:12px;line-height:1.4}

.en-hero__text{margin-top:16px;max-width:520px}
/* 1.5 is the running-text leading for the whole sheet. The sections had drifted
   to five values (1.5 / 1.55 / 1.6 / 1.7 / 1.72) for the same kind of text; the
   measured leading on live Hebrew storefronts sits at 1.43-1.56, and the "1.7 for
   Hebrew" figure traces back to an AI-written skill citing no typographic source. */
.en-hero__text p{margin:0;color:rgb(var(--en-ink)/.82);font-size:17px;line-height:1.5}

/* Square corners, because everything else on this surface is ruled. A pill
   here would be the one soft shape in an instrument panel. */
.en-hero__actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin-top:clamp(18px,2.2vw,26px)}
.en-hero__actions a{
  display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
  min-height:52px;padding:12px 28px;border-radius:0;
  font-weight:600;font-size:16px;text-decoration:none;
  transition:background-color .18s ease,border-color .18s ease,color .18s ease
}
.en-hero__primary{
  border:1px solid rgb(var(--en-ink));
  background:rgb(var(--en-ink));color:rgb(var(--en-night))!important
}
.en-hero__primary:hover{background:#fff;border-color:#fff}
.en-hero__secondary{
  border:1px solid rgb(var(--en-ink)/.58);
  background:transparent;color:rgb(var(--en-ink))!important
}
.en-hero__secondary:hover{border-color:rgb(var(--en-ink));background:rgb(var(--en-ink)/.08)}
.en-hero__actions a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid rgb(var(--en-ink));outline-offset:3px}

/* A schedule of places, ruled and closed on all four sides so it reads as
   part of the panel rather than a table someone forgot to finish. */
/* margin trimmed when the plate scope line was added, so the terms strip
   keeps its measured peek above the fold at 1440x900 and 390x844 */
.en-hero__places{
  display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));
  margin-top:clamp(14px,1.8vw,20px);
  border:1px solid var(--plate-rule);border-block-end:0
}
.en-hero__places a{
  display:flex;align-items:center;min-height:52px;padding:14px 16px;
  border-block-end:1px solid var(--plate-rule);
  color:rgb(var(--en-ink)/.88)!important;text-decoration:none;
  font-size:15px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.3;text-wrap:balance;
  transition:color .18s ease,background-color .18s ease
}
.en-hero__places a+a{border-inline-start:1px solid var(--plate-rule)}
.en-hero__places a:hover{color:rgb(var(--en-ink))!important;background:rgb(var(--en-ink)/.09)}
.en-hero__places a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid rgb(var(--en-ink));outline-offset:-3px}

@media(max-width:900px){
  .en-hero__places{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}
  .en-hero__places a:nth-child(3){border-inline-start:0}
}
@media(max-width:640px){
  .en-hero{min-height:auto}
  .en-plate{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}
  .en-plate__cell:nth-child(3){border-inline-start:0}
  .en-plate__cell:nth-child(n+3){border-top:1px solid var(--plate-rule)}
  .en-hero__actions a{flex:1 1 100%}
  /* Two columns, not one: four stacked rows cost 209px of a 844px screen and
     were the single reason nothing below the hero could show. */
  .en-hero__places{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}
  .en-hero__places a+a{border-inline-start:1px solid var(--plate-rule)}
  .en-hero__places a:nth-child(odd){border-inline-start:0}
  .en-hero__places a{min-height:46px;padding:12px 14px;font-size:14px}
}
/* ── Dusk to lit ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   A solar lamp's entire promise is the transition this photograph is frozen
   inside. Playing that transition on load answers the buyer's first
   objection - "does it actually light anything?" - before a line of copy is
   read, and it demonstrates rather than claims, which is the rule the rest
   of this sheet is built on.

   Both layers animate opacity ONLY. Animating the image's own filter would
   repaint a full-bleed 1456px asset every frame; opacity on a sibling layer
   is composited on the GPU and costs the LCP element nothing. The photograph
   paints at full size immediately - only the veil above it moves.

   Every default state below is the FINISHED state. A visitor with
   reduced-motion, a browser that drops the animation, or a section
   stylesheet that compiles late all land on the intended hero, never on a
   half-dark one. */
.en-hero__dusk{
  position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:-1;pointer-events:none;
  background:rgb(var(--en-night));opacity:0;
  animation:en-dusk-lift 1.45s cubic-bezier(.33,.72,.32,1) both
}
@keyframes en-dusk-lift{from{opacity:.66}to{opacity:0}}

/* Amber here is not an accent and not decoration: it is the light the lamps
   in the photograph emit, which is the one job DESIGN.md licenses amber for.
   Stops are placed on the actual fixtures in the asset - the wall lamp upper
   left, the three-lamp column mid-frame, the string lights over the hedge.
   screen ADDS light instead of laying a film over the image, so the
   photograph stays sharp underneath it.

   These percentages are read off the image file itself
   (elmsnest-hero-desktop-performance.webp, 1456x768), so they are tied to the
   photograph and not to reading direction - RTL must not mirror them. That is
   why they are physical and not logical, per the gradient rule in DESIGN.md. */
.en-hero__glow{
  position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:-1;pointer-events:none;
  mix-blend-mode:screen;opacity:.46;
  background:
    radial-gradient(30% 34% at 18% 25%,rgb(var(--en-amber)/.50) 0%,rgb(var(--en-amber)/.16) 46%,transparent 72%),
    radial-gradient(15% 26% at 40% 47%,rgb(var(--en-amber)/.34) 0%,transparent 70%),
    radial-gradient(22% 12% at 62% 38%,rgb(var(--en-amber)/.30) 0%,transparent 72%);
  animation:en-glow-rise 2.1s ease-out both
}
/* The light holds off until the dark has started lifting, so the two layers
   read as one event - night receding, lamps catching - rather than two. */
@keyframes en-glow-rise{0%,38%{opacity:0}100%{opacity:.46}}

/* Mobile gets no glow at all, and that is a measurement, not a preference.

   The mobile crop puts the path lamp behind the content column, and the plate,
   copy, buttons and schedule together cover most of what is left. An A/B pixel
   diff of the mobile hero with the glow on against the same hero with it
   hidden came back at 1.07 mean delta over 4.66% of pixels - invisible - while
   the same diff on desktop measured 6.78 over 20.49%, concentrated in exactly
   the row bands the wall lamp and the string lights occupy.

   A glow with no visible source is haze, not light. So mobile carries the
   moment on the dusk lift alone, which acts on the whole frame rather than on
   a point and therefore survives the crop. It is set deeper here because the
   mobile asset is already graded lighter (brightness .8, above) and only a
   sliver of it is ever on screen. */
@media(max-width:749px){
  .en-hero__glow{display:none}
  .en-hero__dusk{animation-name:en-dusk-lift-mobile}
}
@keyframes en-dusk-lift-mobile{from{opacity:.80}to{opacity:0}}

/* ── The plate reads one field at a time ─────────────────────────────────
   Four values arriving together are skimmed as a texture; four arriving in
   sequence are read as four measurements, which is the entire point of
   presenting them on a rating plate. Delays are short (.16-.40s) because
   this content is above the fold - a longer stagger would be withholding
   the page's proof, not pacing it.

   7px of travel, ending at rest. DESIGN.md's "nothing lifts" rule governs
   hover, where a lift is a floating-card idiom; an entrance that settles
   into its own cell is a different gesture and stays inside the rule. */
.en-plate__cell{animation:en-field-in .52s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.3,1) both}
.en-plate__cell:nth-child(1){animation-delay:.16s}
.en-plate__cell:nth-child(2){animation-delay:.24s}
.en-plate__cell:nth-child(3){animation-delay:.32s}
.en-plate__cell:nth-child(4){animation-delay:.40s}
@keyframes en-field-in{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(7px)}}

@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
  .en-hero__actions a,.en-hero__places a{transition:none}
  /* Not "instant" versions of the same motion - no motion, final state. */
  .en-hero__dusk,.en-hero__glow,.en-plate__cell{animation:none}
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "ElmsNest hero",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "hdt-section section-allow-transparent",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "תמונת רקע (דסקטופ)" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image_mobile", "label": "תמונת רקע (מובייל)" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "כותרת", "default": "תאורת חוץ סולארית — מה מתאים ומה לא" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "text", "label": "טקסט" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "primary_label", "label": "כפתור ראשי", "default": "לקטלוג המלא" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "secondary_label", "label": "כפתור משני", "default": "לא בטוחים? למדריך הבחירה" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "secondary_url", "label": "קישור כפתור משני", "info": "ברירת מחדל: מדריך בחירת תאורה לגינה" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "ElmsNest hero" }]
}
{% endschema %}
